{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1538662884,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNjY4MTQ1MjU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2896","origin":"github"},"title":"How to handle/provide annex.retry  option?","message":"#### What is the problem?\nApparently the recently added to annex ability to retry failed downloads is disabled (annex.retry defaults to 0) by default.  I first thought that we could just hardcode to provide e.g. `-c annex.retry=3` to all annex calls (`self._ANNEX_GIT_COMMON_OPTIONS`), but then thought that we better have a config setting for it defaulting to 3, BUT this is already git-annex'es config setting, which might be set and we would be forcefully overriding it.  So I wondered what should be our course of action?\n\nI think we could \n- define `datalad.annex.retry` common_cfg defaulting to 3 and describing that it would be used ONLY if configuration is not defining `annex.retry` config option\n- set it in `AnnexRepo.__init__` conditional as described above\n\nSounds like a reasonable plan or am I missing something?","files":null}]}